   permissive license whose text accompanies the Unicode Character Database.

2. tests/data/*_tokenizer_goldens.jsonl, tests/data/*_chat_template_goldens.jsonl

   Generated by tools/gen_tokenizer_goldens.py and
   tools/gen_chat_template_goldens.py by running the reference tokenizer and
   chat template of each model repository over prompts written for this
   project. Each record holds a short rendered string and its token ids: the
   expected output of the reference implementation, kept so this engine's
   tokenizer and template interpreter can be proved to match it. No model
   weights, vocabulary files or template sources are redistributed.

   The reference implementations belong to their publishers:
   unsloth/GLM-5.3-Flash-FP8, Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8 and
   nvidia/GLM-4.7-NVFP4, each under that repository's own license.

3. benchmarks/teacher_text_memorized.txt

   "A Scandal in Bohemia" by Arthur Conan Doyle, first published in 1891 and
   in the public domain. Used as a fixed corpus for teacher-forced perplexity
   comparisons.
